<title>CHILE: Chile December copper exports fall to $532 mln.</title>
<headline>Chile December copper exports fall to $532 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile reported copper exports falling to $531.8 million in December from $605.1 million in the same month in 1995, said the Central Bank in its fortnightly report.</p>
<p>Although export volumes continued to rise, export income was hurt by the sharp fall in world copper prices last year.</p>
<p>Here are details of Chile's mining exports in December.</p>
<p> METAL			   Dec 1996	    Dec 1995</p>
<p> Copper			  531.8		 605.1</p>
<p> Iron				2.8		  10.0</p>
<p> Salitre and iodine	    8.2		  12.1</p>
<p> Silver			   15.1		   8.5</p>
<p> Molybdenum		     25.8		  31.4</p>
<p> Lithium carbonate	     2.6		   2.0</p>
<p> Metallic gold and dore     39.7		  35.1</p>
<p> Gold mineral		    8.0		   0.2</p>
<p> Others			    7.4		   6.4</p>
<p> TOTAL			   641.4		 710.8</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
